Author: pxxD1998 <214340659+pxxD1998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 11 10:01:37 2026 +0800

    fix(sessions): let scroll rebuilds proceed when the picker's anchor is outside the list
    
    Greptile P1 on the routing push (b3a1a52a): with the scroll rebuild routed
    through the background wrapper, scrolling a virtualized sidebar while a
    picker anchored outside the list was open (e.g. opened from a topbar
    title) skipped the row rebuild, so scrolling past the rendered rows
    showed blank space until the picker closed.
    
    The scroll-driven rebuild now checks where the open picker is anchored:
    inside the session list it still defers through the background wrapper;
    outside it the rebuild paints immediately through a
    _repaintSidebarKeepingProjectPicker() variant that keeps the picker (its
    own anchor observer owns its lifecycle) instead of retiring it.
    
    Checked-in regressions: the guard Node case now covers the keep variant
    (no deferral, no retire), and the routing assertions pin the anchor
    check plus both scroll paths. RED on b3a1a52a (2 failures), GREEN after.
    
    Verified locally: five-file gate 125 passed (real Chromium included);
    session/sidebar sweep 1061 passed, 8 skipped; menu/mobile/anchor/touch
    sweep 576 passed, 1 skipped; picker/chip sweep 389 passed; symbol-file
    batch 164 passed; browser keyboard, smoke and new-chat-focus scripts
    pass; npm run lint:runtime, node --check, Ruff on the changed tests and
    git diff --check clean.

