<a href="#"><img alt="P2" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Scroll close check gets lost**

`scheduleReposition` keeps the first event's `closeWhenAway` value. If a viewport event queues a frame and the session list then scrolls the anchor out of view before that frame runs, the scroll request is dropped. Placement runs with `false` and leaves the picker open for an offscreen row. Keep a pending close-check flag and combine later requests before running the frame.
--- greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-10T15:14:03Z tests/test_session_action_menu_focus.py None 31322828a1c6565af966b885aa99c2ec58c3469e
<a href="#"><img alt="P2" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Long-press release goes untested**

`test_picker_deferred_fork_release_keeps_parent_session_in_browser` starts its first touch after the row has already been replaced. That tests a new tap, not releasing the long-press that caused the repaint. It cannot catch differences in where the browser sends the release click when the pressed element disappears.

Start the touch before the handoff, keep it held through the repaint, then release it and check that the next deliberate tap opens the child.
