--- greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-10T20:25:37Z static/sessions.js None 7db9448f844681fcf624f8dbfdd4d28d785eb1af
<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Fork menu uses old state**

When a refresh updates a fork while the picker is open, this early return keeps the old session object as well as the pressed row. The long-press menu can show `Pin` for an already pinned fork, and clicking it sends `pinned: true` instead of unpinning.

Keep the row until release, but resolve the session from the current cache before building the menu.
--- greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-10T20:25:37Z static/sessions.js None 7db9448f844681fcf624f8dbfdd4d28d785eb1af
<a href="#"><img alt="P2" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Escape loses sidebar focus**

This branch leaves the repaint pending until the fork menu closes. On Escape, `closeSessionActionMenu` restores focus first and then rebuilds the sidebar on the next tick. If focus returns to the fork's main button, that button is removed and focus falls back to the page. Keyboard users then lose their place in the sidebar.

After the deferred repaint, restore focus to the replacement control instead.
--- greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-11T01:21:40Z static/sessions.js 10575 2fae04607b10eec04369c0aaf6a8f3cbc7ef321a
<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Replies close the project picker**

The new default removes the picker when an automatic update calls `renderSessionListFromCache()` directly. Expand prior turns in the detailed sidebar, then open “Move to project” before the report request finishes. Both report callbacks still call the renderer directly, so the reply closes the picker while the user is choosing a project. Content-search replies and scroll-driven row rebuilds have the same problem.

Route these automatic repaints through `_repaintSidebarForBackgroundChurn()` before treating every other caller as an explicit action.
--- greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-11T01:41:34Z static/sessions.js None b3a1a52abd7d7eb50ebe3599804f12678faf1eb7
<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Sidebar scrolling shows blank space**

Open “Move to project” from a topbar-title long-press, then scroll a sidebar with more than 80 sessions. The picker is anchored outside `.session-list`, so scrolling the list does not close it. The new `_repaintSidebarForBackgroundChurn()` call skips the row rebuild while that picker remains open. Scrolling beyond the rendered rows then shows blank space instead of conversations until the picker closes.

Let scroll-driven rebuilds proceed when the picker’s anchor is outside the list, or close the picker before rebuilding.
--- greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-11T05:04:08Z static/sessions.js None 54f37973033553057a37bb1bf9d166eb5f69fdf0
<a href="#"><img alt="P2" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Parent menu loses focus**

On touch layouts, `closeSessionActionMenu` can leave focus on the page after closing an expanded parent's menu and replaying the deferred repaint. `ownAction` exists but is hidden by `.session-actions{display:none}`, so this condition skips `row.tabIndex=-1`. The direct `ownMain` is absent, and the replacement row is a plain `div`, so none of the candidates can receive focus.

Make the row focusable before trying it when both controls fail. This is non-blocking, but keyboard users otherwise lose their place in the sidebar.

