<!-- hidden-owner-focus-followup-2026-10-11:start -->
## Review follow-up — hidden owner action focus fallback (2026-10-11)

The latest warm-up and inline review found one remaining non-blocking focus gap on touch layouts. Published `2fae04607b10eec04369c0aaf6a8f3cbc7ef321a` as a history-preserving fast-forward on top of `54f37973033553057a37bb1bf9d166eb5f69fdf0`.

- Deferred menu-close focus restoration now tries the owner's direct controls first, then makes the owning row programmatically focusable only if neither control accepted focus. This covers coarse-pointer layouts where the direct action trigger remains in the DOM under a hidden `.session-actions` container.
- The browser regression fixture now includes that hidden-but-present owner action and still asserts the restored owner ID plus subsequent Enter behavior, preventing focus loss or fork activation.

Verification:

- RED proof: the updated focused regression assertion fails on the previous production source.
- Related menu/session suite: **33 passed, 27 skipped**. The skips are existing Playwright guards because Chromium is unavailable in this runner; the hidden-action browser case is checked in for CI.
- `node --check static/sessions.js`, Ruff on the changed test, and `git diff --check`: clean.
- Uploaded Git tree `8e3e2567b517190b3283e18c85d0b88766459a0d` is byte-identical to the locally tested tree.

Fresh CI and maintainer re-gate remain pending.
<!-- hidden-owner-focus-followup-2026-10-11:end -->

<!-- gate-p1p2p3-followup-2026-10-11:start -->
## Gate follow-up — recovery/rename repaint intent and owner-safe focus (2026-10-11)

The latest exact-head gate reproduced three defects on `c4c8d3cb`; this update fixes all three and was published as history-preserving fast-forward `54f37973033553057a37bb1bf9d166eb5f69fdf0`.

- External `loadSession(..., {externalRefreshReason})` acknowledgements now carry background intent through both metadata and post-message-load repaint points, so transcript recovery preserves an open project picker. Explicit visits still repaint immediately.
- The delayed rename-release repaint now uses the background-churn wrapper, so a held rename response completing after another row opens its picker no longer dismisses that picker.
- Deferred menu-close focus restoration now selects only direct owner controls (`:scope > .session-child-session-main`). A top-level owner with no direct action control becomes programmatically focusable via `tabIndex=-1`, preventing Escape/Enter from transferring activation to the first expanded fork.

Verification:

- RED proof on `c4c8d3cb`: the new background-intent and rename tests failed before the production fix; the owner-focus browser regression also distinguishes the old descendant selector.
- Focused and adjacent suite: **278 passed, 27 skipped** across 18 picker/session/sidebar/unread/rename/focus files. The skips are existing Playwright guards because Chromium is unavailable in this runner; the browser regression is check

